\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces The quenched solid at 300~K. $r_1$, $r_{\min }$ and $r_2$ are the first peak, first minimum and second peak of $g(r)$. Coordination $\bar  {n}$ uses a 2.85~\r A{} cutoff, and ``defects'' is the fraction of atoms that are not fourfold. These columns are computed over the last 50~ps of each equilibration. The MSD column is the plateau value, averaged past 10~ps of the full 150~ps block, since the MSD is measured relative to the first frame of whatever window it is given. No diffusion coefficient is quoted: the MSD is flat, so $D$ is not measurable.}}{40}{table.caption.44}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:quench_structural}{{12}{40}{The quenched solid at 300~K. $r_1$, $r_{\min }$ and $r_2$ are the first peak, first minimum and second peak of $g(r)$. Coordination $\bar {n}$ uses a 2.85~\AA {} cutoff, and ``defects'' is the fraction of atoms that are not fourfold. These columns are computed over the last 50~ps of each equilibration. The MSD column is the plateau value, averaged past 10~ps of the full 150~ps block, since the MSD is measured relative to the first frame of whatever window it is given. No diffusion coefficient is quoted: the MSD is flat, so $D$ is not measurable}{table.caption.44}{}}
